# Docker build context is the repo root (railway.json points at
# backend/Dockerfile, which does `COPY backend/ .`). Without this file that COPY
# sweeps in backend/.env — live LLM keys, the Supabase service key and the DB
# password — and bakes them into an image layer, where they survive even if a
# later layer deletes the file.
#
# Railway builds from the git repo, so .gitignore already keeps .env out of ITS
# context. This is what protects a local `docker build`, which reads the working
# tree and does not consult .gitignore at all.

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Secrets / credentials
*.pem
*.key
**/service-account*.json

# VCS + agent scratch
.git
.gitignore
.agents/
.codex/
.claude/

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled in the image, and copying them
# invalidates the layer cache on every change.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/.vite
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv

# Frontend: the backend image has no use for it
frontend/

# Local noise
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/coverage
